ksu|n|To lay down; to place; to put; to let fall or throw down (as sediment); as, a crocodile deposits her eggs in the sand; the waters deposited a rich alluvium. ; To lay up or away for safe keeping; to put up; to store; as, to deposit goods in a warehouse. ; To lodge in some one's hands for safe keeping; to commit to the custody of another; to intrust; esp., to place in a bank, as a sum of money subject to order. ; To lay aside; to rid one's self of.	a:19ea,61,13;m5a,54,6~19ea,61,13;m5a,54,6	N:19t3,73,7;trb,67,4~19t3,73,7;trb,67,4
