ksz|n|The act of depositing or deposing; the act of laying down or thrown down; precipitation. ; The act of bringing before the mind; presentation. ; The act of setting aside a sovereign or a public officer; deprivation of authority and dignity; displacement; removal. ; That which is deposited; matter laid or thrown down; sediment; alluvial matter; as, banks are sometimes depositions of alluvial matter. ; An opinion, example, or statement, laid down or asserted; a declaration. ; The act of laying down one's testimony in writing; also, testimony laid or taken down in writing, under oath or affirmation, before some competent officer, and in reply to interrogatories and cross-interrogatories.	a:whq,151,30~whq,151,30	V:1elc,120,32;1elf,98,4~1elc,120,32;1elf,98,4	n:u7p,72,10;197i,60,6~u7p,72,10;197i,60,6	N:1elc,70,1~1elc,70,1
